WEBVTT

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:29.900
morning of wednesday august

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:38.020
26, 1992, two grandparents from Wethersfield, Connecticut arrived at Orly Airport outside

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:43.860
of Paris for a celebratory visit to the fabulous capital city of France, where they were to

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:47.420
spend an exciting week with their son David and his family.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:53.670
At the airport, Margaret and Robbins Barstow were warmly greeted by their two grandchildren,

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:59.220
Susanna, age 7, and Jeffrey.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:07.430
age 13, accompanied by son David and his wife, Linda.

00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:10.330
Good to see you. We're here now, huh?

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:11.710
Hello, Dad.

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:16.870
Hello, Dad. How are you?

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:22.980
We're all set. Good.

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:25.240
Yeah, we're all set, and there are the bags.

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:46.670
The Barstow grandparents had come to Paris

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:49.770
to celebrate with their children and grandchildren

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:52.440
their 50th wedding anniversary.

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:56.310
David Barstow, a computer scientist,

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:59.870
had been transferred a year earlier from his job in Austin.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:06.020
texas to work for three years at the paris headquarters of his employing company schlumberger

00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:12.100
so he and his family had found a place to live on the outskirts of paris and we all decided to

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:19.140
make the best of it by having a family reunion in paris to celebrate our anniversary as grandparents

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:27.150
in our 70s we still love to travel but we had never yet done harris so we were greatly excited

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:29.950
at our grandchildren's promise to give us a personal...

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:35.230
tour of this wondrous city of light. Since this was a work day in the middle of the week,

00:03:35.370 --> 00:03:41.130
our first stop was at the large Schlumberger office complex, where David heads up a team

00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:51.780
of six computer research scientists. This is the Schlumberger site in the center of Mont

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:56.230
Rouge, Paris, which is just south of the periphery, so it's technically not part of

00:03:56.230 --> 00:03:57.860
Paris, just over the border.

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:05.820
In that building over there, on the other side of the building, there are actually about

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:10.910
2,000 people here who work at this Schlumberger site, and the Schlumberger Laboratory for Computer

00:04:10.910 --> 00:04:13.900
Science, the European branch, has six of them.

00:04:15.590 --> 00:04:15.910
Right.

00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:16.910
We're headed over this way.

00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:18.310
It has six of those people.

00:04:18.490 --> 00:04:19.230
Six of those 2,000.

